      "description": "<p>We refute the literal unproved k107 product retained in Table 2 of Reznik, Garcia and Koiller's 2020 preprint and 2021 article. Two primitive convex four-periodic billiard trajectories in the ellipse with semiaxes 4 and 3, sharing the same strictly nested confocal elliptical caustic, give exact values 288/625 and 625/1152 for (A'/A) times the product of original internal half-angle sines. A self-contained continuous-family proof checks physical reflection, strict caustic contact interiors and all denominators.</p><p>The general four-periodic construction, its caustic and area identities are credited to Garcia and Reznik. Ferudun's contemporary note (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23075934) contains the same exact correction and is explicitly cited. The original repository disclosure has September 30, 2026 provider dates, before the retrieved October 1 deposit; no exclusive priority or independent discovery is claimed. A bounded primary-source audit and its separately unidentified in-preparation manuscript access limit are disclosed. No corrected all-period invariant is asserted.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in developing, drafting, reproducing and adversarially verifying this work. This preprint is unrefereed and has not undergone conventional human peer review. The support archive includes standalone source, provenance, priority comparisons and portable exact rational and symbolic diagnostics. Diagnostics support the proof and are not proof-assistant formalization.</p>",
